  "solution": {
    "text": "<p>Bromobenzene is treated with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>conc</mi><mo>.</mo><mo> </mo><msub><mi>HNO</mi><mn>3</mn></msub></math> to give <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mn>2</mn><mo>, 4, 6 </mo><mi>trinitrophenol</mi></math> by electrophilic substitution reaction mechanism, which on reaction with <math xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1998/Math/MathML\"><mi>NaOH</mi></math> give trinitrophenol. It is also known as picric acid.</p><p><img src=\"https://cdn-question-pool.getmarks.app/pyq/jee_main/d843583a-718a-49ad-9b49-23041d60758f.png\" style=\"width: 734px; height: 451px;\"/></p>",
